      <h1>How to Calculate and Read a <em>Z-Score</em></h1>
      <p class="dek">A z-score says how many standard deviations a value sits from the mean, which turns scores measured on completely different scales into numbers you can compare directly. The arithmetic is a single line. The part worth getting right is what the number means, and when the percentile it implies can be trusted.</p>
